  "setup": "Each sequence starts on a card that is LOADED by CREATE with the right access hash (any 32-byte value; the wrong access hash is any other value), followed by a new OPEN: f = 0, waited = 0, not verified. After every step the replayer sends STATUS in the current session and compares its response with status (life(1) \u2016 tries(1), \u00a79.3); STATUS has no side effect. A step with repeat n is sent n times, each answered with sw; status is checked after the last one.",
  "tear": "after-T-FAIL: power is lost after the T-FAIL transaction of this VERIFY committed and before any later persistent write (\u00a79.5 steps 5-9). The command has no response (sw torn); the replayer powers the card up, SELECTs the wallet applet and OPENs a new session before the STATUS check.",
